<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Martí</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1853">1853</a>–<a href="/years/1895">1895</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Martí was a Cuban poet, journalist and revolutionary, the national hero of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>. Exiled for most of his life, mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolutionary-party">Cuban Revolutionary Party</a> in 1892 to unite the exiles for a new war of independence. He was killed at Dos Ríos on 19 May 1895, soon after landing in Cuba, and his writings shaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American modernismo and Cuban nationalism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-marti.jpg" alt="José Martí" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cuba. Secretaría de Instrucción Pública y Bellas Artes. · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Mart%C3%AD_retrato_hecho_en_M%C3%A9xico_1875.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
